---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import ProjectPage from '../../components/ProjectPage.astro'
import PixelArtBush from '../../components/PixelArtBush.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <ProjectPage title="Pixel art bush">
    <PixelArtBush slot="project-code" />

    <Fragment slot="project-description">
      <p>Time to play with textures now !</p>
      <p>
        I wanted to make my own textures for these little bushes, and took a bit
        of inspiration from HD-2D games aesthetics. So we have 2 kind of
        materials in this scene : MeshStandardMaterial for the ground and the
        small grass leaves and MeshBasicMaterial with transparency enabled for
        the bushes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The bushes and grass are simple PlaneGeometries, while the ground is
        made from 2 CylinderGeometries of different sizes and color.
      </p>
      <p>
        As for the ramen bowl scene, I used very simple lights : one
        AmbientLight, one HemisphereLight and one PointLight.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ProjectPage>
</Layout>
